Package: dinero-core
Architecture: any
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
 adduser,
Description: Dinero (DIN) full node and CLI
 Dinero Core ships dinerod (the full node), dinero-cli (the RPC
 client), dinero-backup (wallet/shielded recovery tool), and
 dinero-prepare-upgrade (rollback binary capture).
 .
 Phase E.3: RocksDB, Boost, secp256k1-zkp, jsoncpp, and OpenSSL are
 statically linked from third_party/ vendoring. GPU mining and
 hardware-wallet HID support are excluded from the packaged daemon
 (separate desktop / miner packages will ship those). The entire
 gRPC stack (libgrpc++, libprotobuf, abseil, c-ares, re2) is
 excluded via DINERO_RELEASE=ON because the current gRPC server
 has not had TLS/mTLS landed; revisit when Lightning is actually
 shipping. ${shlibs:Depends} therefore narrows to base-system
 packages only.
 .
 See /usr/share/doc/dinero/dinero.conf.example for configuration
 keys and /usr/share/doc/dinero/dinero.service.example for a
 manual-mode systemd unit. The package itself ships
 /lib/systemd/system/dinero.service for packaged-service mode.
 The unit is installed but NOT auto-enabled; run
 `systemctl enable --now dinero` to start the service.
